WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You directed
the horror movie of the year.

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.502 line:92%
Not just the movie of the year

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the horror movie
of the year.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you have long
been a fan of horror.

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:07.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
Back in the day, we saw plenty
of horror movies together.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:10.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're a fan of Tim Burton.
-Yes.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
Big fan of Tim Burton
growing up.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Beetlejuice"
is a big movie for you?

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
What do you got there?

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.584 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:20.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, this is just my taxes.
-Okay. All right.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
All right, hold on to that.
-So how old --

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is you dressing up
as Beetlejuice.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's me.
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:29.963 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Pretty great.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:32.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I used the same costume
for Garth,

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:35.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
from "Wayne's World,"
the next year.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.269 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.270 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah, so that's --

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just got me
un-laid by my own wife.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:40.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-By showing that.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This moved you backwards.
Yeah, this moved you this far.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:46.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is you laid,
and then, I just did this.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:49.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:49.883 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's great.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.385
But that's young to have seen
"Beetlejuice," I feel like.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it was --
It scared me.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:55.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, okay, good.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
She takes the face off.
No, it was --

00:00:57.357 --> 00:01:01.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, that's one of the things
I loved about Tim Burton

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that he entertained
and scared at the same time.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just
has this very specific mix.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.268 line:92%
So hats off to you, Tim Burton.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Michael Keaton
just literally

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the greatest
actors alive.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Amazing performance.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I wonder
how Michael Keaton feels

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.010 line:92%
that, like, his entire life --

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.212 size:81% position:41%
He's put some amazing
performances together,

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:21.014
and people must
just be like "Beetlejuice, man."

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Aah!"
"I didn't --

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't do the face thing.
That was prosthetics."

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No, you did it."
Yeah.

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:30.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Do you have people say,
'Do the face thing'?"

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Do it, do it!"
Yeah.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:35.028
-You had fantastic actors
in your film, as well.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:35.662 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Daniel Kaluuya,
who's fantastic.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
Keener, Bradley Whitford.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.266 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-And Allison Williams.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.469 size:75% position:38%
And Allison Williams
was here recently,

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:44.337 line:92%
and I heard that she came to you

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she needed help
with a scene.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:50.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. So this --
One day, she just --

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.177 line:92%
She calls me, and she says --

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, there's
a love scene in the movie.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not like a hot,
steamy sex scene.

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:58.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would not feel comfortable
directing that.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just don't --
That's not my style.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it was like this soft,
sweet love scene,

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she calls me,
and she's like,

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:06.960
"Look, I really need to practice
that love scene with Daniel,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.162 line:92%
and I'm gonna invite him over.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:11.464
Can you come and, like --
Can we work this out?"

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
This was like
my worst nightmare.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:14.634 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.768 line:92%
"Like, okay, so I have to go --

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:18.605
Okay, I have to go to your house
and like witness you

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
doing this weird love --
like direct it?

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:21.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, come on.
This is --"

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:25.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, just absolute --
absolute nightmare.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.012 line:92%
"Okay, I'm a director now.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:29.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm an enigmatic,
intelligent director.

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:30.483 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I have to man up.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:33.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I went over to the house,
and, of course,

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.622 line:92%
it was a surprise party for me.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience "Awws" ]
-Oh, that's fantastic.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was very sweet.
At which point I realized,

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:42.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
of course, Allison Williams
does not need coaching

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
with love scenes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's fine.
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:49.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She also told me,
which sounded fantastic,

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:52.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that, again,
your unique situation,

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you're a director,
not only an actor

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:57.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
but an incredible
sketch performer, as well,

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.879
that you would sometimes direct,
if it called for it,

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
as Tracy Morgan
and sometimes as Barack Obama.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.654
If you needed to pick up
the room a little bit, you know,

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:08.354 size:78% position:39% line:92%
you can just be like,

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:09.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ As Obama ]
"All right, now, and cut!

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.391 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
All right, let's...

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:14.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
that's pretty good.

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:15.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's pretty good."

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:18.565 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.266 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"But it's, uh...

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we can do
a little bit better."

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.636 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Let's learn our lines,
for starters.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:27.674 size:81% position:41% line:92%
That'd be a big help."

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:29.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
this is one of those things

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
where, like,
the audience is ready for this

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.580 size:81% position:41% line:92%
to go to a punch line.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.747 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:35.615 line:92%
It's not. it's just a voice.

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Punch line --
When would you direct --

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:39.586
What would be the scene you
would need Tracy Morgan for?

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:43.890
-Tracy Morgan was somehow a more
competent director than Obama.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ As Tracy Morgan ]
"All right, stop, let's go!

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:47.660 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hey, let's go!

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody, let's get this --
We're gonna be movin'.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:52.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got to be there
in 60 seconds!"

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:52.832 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:57.804 size:88% position:44%
"We got to be there --"
Tracy -- Tracy is, uh --

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.339 line:92%
Tracy's a good friend of mine.

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:00.440 line:92%
He's like a brother to me.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.641 size:81% position:41%
-And you're producing
a show with him, yeah?

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:05.445
-I'm producing a show with him,
starring him, Tiffany Haddish.

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:06.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, fantastic.
-Cedric the Entertainer.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
Amazing cast.
-That's incredible.

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:11.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's on TBS.
It's called "The Last O.G."

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:11.884 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:16.256
-And it's just a super funny
show, and Tracy is amazing.

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one day --
This is --

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was talking to him
on the phone,

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.760 line:92%
and he was eating something.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.794 size:81% position:41% line:92%
He's like, "Mm. Sorry.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm eating a Ding Dong
right now."

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:24.631 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:27.800
Like, "All right, no problem,"
And he starts talking to me.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:31.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
All of a sudden,
he starts coughing violently.

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:32.972 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Coughing loudly ]

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like,
"Tracy, are you okay?"

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:36.509 line:92%
[ Coughing ] "Yeah, yeah.

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:37.744 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm Tracy Morgan.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:41.014
Survived getting hit by a truck,
killed by a Ding Dong!"

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:44.350 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:47.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
Classic line.
-Well, I can't wait for that.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:47.654 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:50.023
-I can't wait for everything
that's coming next for you.

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:52.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm just an audience
that can't wait for more.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations on everything
this year, Jordan.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:55.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you, man.
-It's just fantastic.

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:57.363 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Jordan Peele, everybody!

